"""Host-only controls for the VM harness (#659's streams; no guest, no device).

    python3 -I tools/vm-harness-test                     # every case, against this checkout's tools
    python3 -I tools/vm-harness-test --case exit-skip    # one case (repeatable)
    python3 -I tools/vm-harness-test --tools-from DIR    # the tools under test from DIR (an unfixed export)

Each case copies the tool under test into a scratch root of its own under
.qa-scratch/t12/vm-harness-test/ beside doubles of its siblings
(cloud-test-backend, vm-pair) and puts ssh and scp doubles first on PATH.
The doubles answer from a table the case writes and log every call. Nothing
runs against a guest, a device or a cloud; TMPDIR is the scratch root's, so
nothing is written under /tmp. A case prints PASS or FAIL with its reason;
the run exits 1 when any case failed.
"""
